1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,108
Picture a Mezo borrower at a safe ratio.

2
00:00:04,108 --> 00:00:11,811
A redemption takes their BTC anyway, sold
at one dollar per MUSD, because their loan

3
00:00:11,811 --> 00:00:13,865
was first in line.

4
00:00:13,865 --> 00:00:17,973
On Mezo mainnet, redemptions
hit loans 1,310 times.

5
00:00:17,973 --> 00:00:19,000
Liquidations, 28.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,333
Frontline is a redemption market for MUSD.

7
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:29,000
Borrowers pay a small premium, and BTC
holders called absorbers stand first in line.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
This is Mezo’s redemption line,
read live from the chain.

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Pick a size and see where it stops.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
I lock 0.2 BTC and borrow 6,000 MUSD.

11
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:49,500
Before I sign, I see the absorber
debt in front of me, and the premium:

12
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:51,000
half a percent.

13
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:59,793
Someone redeems 5,000 MUSD, here on a
local fork of Mezo testnet with the real

14
00:00:59,793 --> 00:01:00,379
contracts.

15
00:01:00,379 --> 00:01:05,069
The absorber loan drops
from 30,347 to 25,347.

16
00:01:05,069 --> 00:01:08,000
My loan does not move.

17
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Absorbers earn the premium.

18
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:18,500
A redemption swaps part of their BTC for
MUSD at the oracle price, with no loss in

19
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:19,000
dollars.

20
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,368
Frontline does not change MUSD.

21
00:01:21,368 --> 00:01:27,053
Our contracts own real troves and
keep absorber loans at the front.

22
00:01:27,053 --> 00:01:30,842
Thirty-six tests run against
the real MUSD contracts;

23
00:01:30,842 --> 00:01:35,105
a self-review fixed one
high and two medium issues.

24
00:01:35,105 --> 00:01:37,000
Wallets use Mezo Passport.

25
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:37,500
Next:

26
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:42,000
outside users on testnet,
then a capped mainnet launch.

27
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,000
So redemptions take BTC only from
those who chose to be first.
